panfrost: a collision-free hash for the CRC clear colour

pan_pack_color() repeats a packed clear value over all four words for every format narrower than
128 bits, and the upstream pan_crc_clear_color_hash_rt() (per-channel products of four primes
combined with XOR) then hashes different clear colours alike: on R8G8B8A8_UNORM (0, 6/255, 0, 1)
and (0, 10/255, 0, 1) give the same crc_clear_color. Transaction elimination then reads the stored
CRC of empty tiles as unchanged and skips writing the new clear colour. The hash runs the render
target index and each packed word in turn through a 64-bit mix (the SplitMix64 finalizer) and
keeps the 46 bits pan_crc_clear_color_pack() has room for; two different clear values share a hash
with odds of 2^-46.

--- a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_desc.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_desc.h
@@ -367,20 +367,37 @@ pan_effective_tile_block_size(unsigned tile_size)
 }
 
 #if PAN_ARCH >= 7
+static inline uint64_t
+pan_crc_clear_color_mix64(uint64_t x)
+{
+   /* A 64-bit bijection that spreads every input bit over the result (the
+    * finalizer of the SplitMix64 generator). */
+   x = (x ^ (x >> 30)) * 0xbf58476d1ce4e5b9ull;
+   x = (x ^ (x >> 27)) * 0x94d049bb133111ebull;
+   return x ^ (x >> 31);
+}
+
 static inline uint64_t
 pan_crc_clear_color_hash_rt(unsigned rt, const uint32_t clear[4])
 {
-   /* The prime number 16381 is carefully selected so that the 32 bits
-    * of each clear color channel take at most 46 bits after the mul (the next
-    * prime number 16411 takes at most 47 bits). The resulting hash value is
-    * guaranteed not to overflow and can safely be packed. */
-   static const uint64_t primes[4] = {16381ULL, 16369ULL, 16363ULL, 16361ULL};
-   uint64_t hash = 0;
+   /* A hash of the render target index and its four packed clear words,
+    * cut to the 46 bits pan_crc_clear_color_pack() has room for. Two
+    * different clear values share a hash with odds of 2^-46.
+    *
+    * Each word goes through the 64-bit mix in turn. Summing per-channel
+    * products of fixed primes with XOR instead collides whenever the four
+    * words hold the same value, as pan_pack_color() gives every format
+    * narrower than 128 bits: on R8G8B8A8_UNORM the clears (0, 6/255, 0, 1)
+    * and (0, 10/255, 0, 1) hashed alike, so a render pass clearing a target
+    * to the second colour after one had cleared it to the first left the
+    * tiles with no primitives on them in the first colour (transaction
+    * elimination took them as unchanged). */
+   uint64_t hash = pan_crc_clear_color_mix64(rt + 1);
 
    for (unsigned c = 0; c < 4; c++)
-      hash ^= primes[c] * clear[c] * (rt + 1);
+      hash = pan_crc_clear_color_mix64(hash ^ clear[c]);
 
-   return hash;
+   return hash & ((1ull << 46) - 1);
 }
 
 static inline uint64_t
